  "requirement": "Carries an I/O failure or a diagnostic for invalid source input, such as an unknown language or invalid UTF-8 in a request for text.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum SourceError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Invalid(String),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Debug for SourceError;\nimpl Display for SourceError;\nimpl Error for SourceError;\nimpl From<std::io::Error> for SourceError;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations** from `requirements.sdk.sources.SourceError`:\n- The enum has an `Io(std::io::Error)` variant and an `Invalid(String)` variant.\n- `Invalid` carries a diagnostic for invalid source input. The text gives two examples: an unknown language and invalid UTF-8 in a request for text.\n- It implements `Debug`, `Display`, `Error` and `From<std::io::Error>`.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- `Invalid` display: `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[invalid_source_errors_display_the_diagnostic]` builds `SourceError::Invalid(\"unsupported source language\")` and asserts `to_string()` equals that diagnostic exactly.\n- Invalid UTF-8: `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[source_bytes_error_kinds_and_language_names_round_trip]` reads the bytes `[0xff, 0xfe]` and asserts `binary.text()` returns `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` with a non-empty message.\n- `From<io::Error>` and the `Io` variant: the same test calls `SourceError::from(io::Error::other(\"unreadable source\"))`. It asserts the result matches `SourceError::Io(_)` and that `to_string()` is `\"unreadable source\"`. This covers the `Io` variant, the `From` conversion and `Display` for `Io`.\n- Unknown language: the same test runs `sources.search_structure` with `LanguageId` `\"CustomLang\"`. It asserts `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` where the message contains `CustomLang`.\n\n**Trait impls not asserted directly**\n- `Debug` is `#[derive(Debug)]` on `enum[SourceError]` in `src/sources/public.rs`. Tests also call `.unwrap()` on `Result<_, SourceError>`, which requires `Debug`.\n- `impl std::error::Error for SourceError {}` in `src/sources/public.rs` is an empty impl. It has no conditional and no transformation, so the exemption for untested obligations applies. It is also used as a trait bound in generic code.\n\n**Gaps:** I found none. Each variant, its conversion, its `Display` output and the two named invalid-input cases are exercised with real assertions. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` is marked for the public API requirement and only supplements the above.",
